# Unit Testing

We use unit tests **sparingly**. All non-configuration logic belongs in **Domain** and **Application** — that is what we test.

## Test Project

- `NTierTemplate.Test/` references **Domain**, **Application**, and **Data** (Data is referenced only for DAO interface types used in mocks)
- Do not reference Api, Cli, Queue, or Web from the test project

## What to Test

- Domain entity behavior and value-object logic
- Application service use-case orchestration (mock DAO interfaces from `NTierTemplate.Data/`)

## What Not to Test

- Configuration and wiring: IoC registration, `Program.cs`, host bootstrap, `appsettings`, EF configuration, DAO implementations, migrations
- Entry-point hosts (Api, Cli, Queue) — thin hosts with no business logic
- Data layer persistence — exercised through integration/manual verification, not unit tests here

## Conventions

- Mock DAO interfaces (`IUserDao`, etc.) when testing Application services — use **Moq**; never mock EF or Identity types
- Use **FluentAssertions** for expectations (`value.Should().Be(...)`, `collection.Should().Contain(...)`, etc.)
- Add tests only when they protect meaningful behavior; do not test trivial getters or framework boilerplate
- Keep test types and methods domain-named, matching the code under test

